B = [
('Lotus', 'Europe', '1960s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Lotus, lightweight, stripped-back and purposeful British racing minimalism. Thin moulded shells in low wedge or rounded teardrop outlines, with bare edges, wide swelling curves and nothing added that is not needed. Racing green is paired with a single bright yellow band, alongside black with gold pinstriping, white, orange and metallic silver. A small round badge in green and yellow with intertwined initials in a circle acts as the recurring mark. Lettering is clean, wide-spaced capitals, often in gold on black. Surfaces are glossy fibreglass-like sheen, exposed aluminium and thin carbon weave. Colour blocking is simple, sharp and light in spirit.'),
('Peugeot', 'Europe', '1980s-2000s', 'cars', 'In the style of Peugeot, neat, compact, well-proportioned French design with a sporty tidy hand. Clean wedge-like outlines, smooth uncluttered surfaces with a single crisp crease, black plastic edging and slim wraparound shapes. A shield-shaped emblem holds a roaring lion head in polished silver on black, repeated as the signature mark. Lettering is upright, evenly spaced capitals in white or chrome. Palette is white, bright red, ocean blue, silver, dark green and black, with fine grey detailing. Materials include glossy enamel paint, deep-pile cloth, grey textured plastic and brushed chrome. Practical, lively and carefully balanced.'),
('Bugatti', 'Europe', '1930s', 'cars', 'In the style of Bugatti, sensuous, artistic, aristocratic art deco sculpture. Flowing swept curves, teardrop and horseshoe outlines, fine parallel louvre lines and elegant tapering forms with a polished metal spine. A small red oval badge with white capital lettering and a ring of tiny dots serves as the mark. Palette is French racing blue, black over red, deep cream, ivory and two-tone schemes. Finishes are nickel-polished metal, engine-turned aluminium in tight repeating swirls, soft red or brown leather and deep lacquer. Lettering is tall, narrow, stylised deco capitals in vertical stacks. Geometric sunburst and stepped motifs appear on flat graphic surfaces.'),
('Maserati', 'Europe', '1960s-present', 'cars', 'In the style of Maserati, graceful, smooth, refined Italian grand touring elegance. Long flowing outlines, tight sloping curves, wide sculpted shoulders and boomerang-like accents with restrained, polished surfaces. A three-pronged trident emblem in chrome, silver or black is the recurring mark, often set on a deep red or royal blue field. Palette is deep blue, silver, dark burgundy, pearl white and black. Finishes are mirror chrome, pearl lacquer, polished wood, carbon weave and tan, red or cream leather with fine contrast stitching. Lettering is wide-spaced, light capitals with a luxurious calm. Details are few, precise and quietly expensive.'),
('Fiat', 'Europe', '1950s-70s', 'cars', 'In the style of Fiat, tiny, round, cheerful and playful post-war Italian design. Bulbous egg-like and bubble forms, softly curved tops, thin chrome edges and simple rounded rectangles. Square or round badges in red with white capital lettering and small crossed bar marks give a friendly, repeated emblem. Palette is pastel yellow, powder blue, mint green, cream, cherry red, orange and white, often in flat, single-colour fields. Surfaces are painted body-colour metal, simple vinyl, canvas and lightly polished chrome. Lettering is bold, rounded, slightly condensed sans-serif capitals. Flat vintage illustration blocks with simple shapes and bright optimistic colour make everything feel light and sunny.'),
('Saab', 'Europe', '1970s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Saab, aeronautical, quirky, practical and eccentric Swedish design. Short, stubby, rounded forms with deeply curved glass-like surfaces, rectangular accents and a cockpit-like compactness. A round deep-blue enamel disc ringed in chrome carries a crowned red griffin head with white capital lettering, and is the signature mark. Palette is midnight blue, black, silver metallic, deep red and white. Finishes are satin black plastic edges, brushed alloy with a distinct pattern of round holes, grey or blue textured cloth and moulded rubbery trims. Lettering is plain, wide, evenly spaced sans-serif capitals. Asymmetric wraparound forms with big round faces give a functional, jet-inspired character.'),
('Skoda', 'Europe', '1960s-80s', 'cars', 'In the style of Skoda, small, plain, boxy, honest and rugged Czech design. Flat surfaces, round and softly squared forms, chrome-rimmed edges, slim outlines and smooth unfussy bodies with no ornament beyond one proud mark. A round emblem holds a winged arrow in a ring, in black, silver and green, or in older blue and white versions, often as a small enamel pin or raised metal badge. Palette is pale beige, olive green, sky blue, mustard yellow and brick red, with black and silver. Materials are plain vinyl, flat grey or brown plastic, painted steel and simple chrome. Lettering is square-ish, sturdy capitals. Modest, utilitarian and unpretentious.'),
('Dodge', 'North America', '1970s', 'cars', 'In the style of Dodge, brutal, loud, cartoonish tough-guy American muscle of the early 1970s. Wide, aggressive, squared-off forms with bulging humps, a pronounced hip curve, and a bold bumblebee band or thick vertical stripes wrapped around the body. Stripes are black over yellow, red, orange or grey, sometimes with a ducktail kick shape. A round badge and a ram motif act as marks. Surfaces are slotted metal textures, glossy high-impact paint, black vinyl and chunky proportions. Palette is violet, lime green, purple, bright orange, pale green, yellow and black. Lettering is heavy, blocky, slanted capitals with stencilled hard edges. Swaggering, noisy and showy.'),
('Chrysler', 'North America', '1957-1960s', 'cars', 'In the style of Chrysler, late 1950s and early 60s forward-look American design, space-age, optimistic and airy. Long slender profiles, tall swept-back blade shapes, V-shaped winged ornaments, and flowing chrome side strips that divide contrasting colour panels. A chrome five-pointed star within a pentagon, and wing-like badges in polished gold or silver, are the recurring marks. Surfaces are mirror chrome, sculpted pressed panels, glossy lacquer and luxurious woven fabric. Palette is turquoise, flamingo pink, cream, charcoal, red and gold. Lettering is flowing script and tall chrome capitals. Push-button crispness and confident, uplifting streamlining.'),
('Lincoln', 'North America', '1960s', 'cars', 'In the style of Lincoln, understated, sober, expensive American flagship luxury of the 1960s. Slab-sided, perfectly flat surfaces, a thin knife-edge horizontal line, long level forms and a square, formal outline. A four-pointed star set within a plain rectangle or a round enamel plaque is the repeated mark, in chrome, navy and black, with elegant flowing script lettering and a small leaping hound motif. Minimal chrome comes in a thin shoulder strip, slim vertical forms and fine horizontal bars. Brushed metal and deep leather give grave dignity. Palette is black, midnight blue, silver, white and a touch of gold.'),
]
